Description: pvr: limit z replication to subpasses with a free color output
 When a depth attachment written in a render is read as an input attachment
 by a subpass merged into the same render, the hardware setup in
 pvr_arch_hw_pass.c replicates the depth into color storage
 (pvr_enable_z_replicate()). The fragment shader of a writing subpass stores
 the replicated depth to the output location FRAG_RESULT_DATA0 + color_count
 (pvr_init_fs_outputs(), pvr_setup_fs_outputs() in pvr_arch_pipeline.c), and
 the load op shader to FRAG_RESULT_DATA0 + z_replicate, where z_replicate
 counts the color attachments and the on-chip input attachments of the
 subpass (pvr_copy_z_replicate_details(), pvr_uscgen_loadop() in
 pvr_usc.c). The tile buffer flags of these locations are kept in the 8 bit
 masks output_tile_buffers (pco_data.h). An index of 8 or more selects
 FRAG_RESULT_DUAL_SRC_BLEND, whose stores nir_lower_blend() removes
 (consume_dual_stores()), loses its tile buffer flag, and from 9 on is past
 the end of pco_fs_data::outputs[]. With at most 4 color and 4 input
 attachments this can only happen for 4 + 4; with 8 color attachments every
 subpass that writes the replicated depth would hit it.
 .
 Only replicate the depth if every subpass of the render that writes it has
 fewer than PVR_MAX_COLOR_ATTACHMENTS color and input attachments together.
 Otherwise the subpass is not merged and reads the depth from memory, as is
 already done for a stencil input attachment. A subpass that reads its own
 depth attachment and has no room for the replica reads it from memory as
 well. Nothing changes for subpasses with less than 8 color and input
 attachments.
 .
 Only for this downstream stack; not intended for upstream submission.
